  "notes": "{汚|よご}す is a transitive godan verb meaning \"to make dirty\" or \"to pollute.\"\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{汚|よご}れる→汚れる：01293_yogoreru⟧ (intransitive - to get dirty)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {汚|よご}して⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧: is in the process of dirtying\n- {汚|よご}して⟦ある→ある：00006_aru⟧: has been intentionally dirtied\n\nCOMMON OBJECTS:\n- ⟦{服|ふく}→服：00695_fuku⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{汚|よご}す: to dirty clothes\n- ⟦{部屋|へや}→部屋：00507_heya⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{汚|よご}す: to make a room messy\n- ⟦{空気|くうき}→空気：01390_kuuki⟧/⟦{川|かわ}→川：02186_kawa⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{汚|よご}す: to pollute air/river\n- ⟦{名誉|めいよ}→名誉：10568_meiyo⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{汚|よご}す: to tarnish one's honor\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n⟦{手|て}→手：00569_te⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{汚|よご}す has two meanings:\n1. Literal: to dirty one's hands\n2. Figurative: to do something immoral/criminal",
